Z||000000||Santa Cruzer||08-04-2001||03:30 PM||||its located on one of the rocket covers the hose that supposidly dosen't filter good air back to the motor? any pics?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||08-04-2001||03:38 PM||||Don't have any pics, but the V-6 PCV inlet hose was changed as part of a recall. <BR>The original hose went from a fitting on the front valve cover, to a rubber hose, to a 3/4" pipe on the firewall. A hose on the other end of that pipe went to the air filter housing. <BR>The new (recall) configuration is a metal pipe that plugs into the front valve cover and the black rubber intake duct, just before the throttle body.<BR>If yours has had the recall, make sure that the fitting on the air filter housing is plugged, or your engine will inhale unfiltered air through it. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||08-04-2001||03:43 PM||||Santa Cruzer, I believe you are refering to a hose that was off the firewall side of the V6. It ran to a steel pipe on the firewall and on to the air intake on the drivers side.<BR>Usually the pipe is still there with the hose cut. I removed the metal pipe to get a little extra space  when working on the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Santa Cruzer||08-04-2001||03:46 PM||||there is a pipe i have no idea what it's 4 and it goes tot he firewall i belive and it's not hooked up... it leadsto no hoses or anythign its just there.. is this a problem?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||08-04-2001||05:16 PM||||Nope, no problem.||||reg||1
Z||000005||WisconsinGT||08-05-2001||12:05 PM||||Raydar, What do you mean when you say: "If yours has had the recall, make sure that the fitting on the air filter housing is plugged, or your engine will inhale unfiltered air through it. " Do you have picts of this? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||08-05-2001||12:35 PM||||Sorry, no pics. But if you look near the bottom of the air filter housing, near the end of the pipe on the firewall, there may be a fitting where the hose used to go. <BR>If you take the lid off the air filter housing and take out the filter element, you should be able to see if there are any small hose fittings on the housing. Just make sure any unused ones are capped. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||11
