Z||000010||AL||08-06-2001||01:55 AM||||if it is dirty air well isn't that what the air filter is for? ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Indiana_resto_guy||08-06-2001||02:21 AM||||Al, if you look at where the air is being introduced to the system, you should note that it is in the area that by-passes the air filter.<BR>Result, un-filtered air being mixed with filtered air. The air filter then is not doing much good.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||08-06-2001||11:19 AM||||The unfiltered air enters the center of the air filter element, through the bottom of the can. Everything on the outside of the can is supposed to be sealed. If the outside of the can is open to the atmosphere, you're breathing unfiltered air.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
